,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.30719268,"data":"What is $1-1$? You have access to `math`, `numpy`, and `sympy` for:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307194753,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307196919,"data":"# Symbolic Computation (sympy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307200378,"data":"- Algebraic manipulation and simplification\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307202474,"data":"- Solving equations and systems of equations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307208306,"data":"- Symbolic differentiation and integration\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307210101,"data":"- Number theory functions (primes, divisors, modular arithmetic)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307212094,"data":"- Polynomial operations and factorization\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307214302,"data":"- Working with mathematical expressions symbolically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307216258,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307218002,"data":"# Numerical Computation (numpy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307219776,"data":"- Array operations and linear algebra\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307221734,"data":"- Efficient numerical calculations for large datasets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307223614,"data":"- Matrix operations and eigenvalue problems\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307225695,"data":"- Statistical computations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307227692,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307229616,"data":"# Mathematical Functions (math):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.30723159,"data":"- Standard mathematical functions (trig, log, exp)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307233542,"data":"- Constants like pi and e\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307235452,"data":"- Basic operations for single values\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307290187,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307292508,"data":"Best Practices:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307294385,"data":"- Use sympy for exact symbolic answers when possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307296294,"data":"- Use numpy for numerical verification and large-scale computation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307298156,"data":"- Combine symbolic and numerical approaches: derive symbolically, verify numerically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307300102,"data":"- Document your computational strategy clearly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307302183,"data":"- Validate computational results against known cases or theoretical bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307304112,"data":"- For very large exponents (e.g. a^(n!)), use pow(base, exp, mod) or analytical methods — never materialize the full number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307306426,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307308113,"data":"# Code Robustness Rules:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307310221,"data":"- Each code cell must be SELF-CONTAINED: re-import and re-define everything you need. If a previous cell errored, its definitions are LOST.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307312202,"data":"- Avoid sympy expressions that grow beyond a few hundred characters. If an expression is exploding, switch to numerical methods (numpy) or modular arithmetic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307314268,"data":"- For geometry: prefer numpy coordinate models with brute-force verification over pure symbolic or direction-counting approaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307316464,"data":"- For combinatorics counting: always verify no duplicates — check injectivity explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307318562,"data":"- If 5+ code cells without progress, STOP and restart with a different approach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307320587,"data":"- When using Python, prefer converting sympy expressions to int() before passing to Python builtins like pow(), min(), max().\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307322851,"data":"- Common import: from sympy.ntheory.modular import crt (note: sympy.crt does not exist).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.3073282,"data":"- If a code cell fails, re-import necessary libraries in the next cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307331002,"data":"- sympy.solve() often times out on complex systems. For polynomial systems with \u003e 3 unknowns, prefer numerical methods (scipy fsolve/minimize) or manual algebraic reduction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307333327,"data":"- Never call sympy.simplify() or sympy.expand() on expressions involving large binomials or products of many terms. Use float() first to check the numerical value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.30733553,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307337263,"data":"# Library Availability:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307339361,"data":"NOT installed (do NOT import — they WILL fail): pulp, ortools, z3-solver, mip, pyscipopt, pysat, cvxpy, constraint, matplotlib, sklearn.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307341508,"data":"Do not waste turns trying these libraries or probing with try/except.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307343682,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307345545,"data":"Available and recommended:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.30734751,"data":"- sympy, numpy, scipy, networkx, mpmath, math, itertools, functools, fractions, collections, decimal, heapq, random, statistics\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307349902,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.30735198,"data":"Replacements for unavailable optimization/constraint libraries:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307354178,"data":"- Integer/Binary Linear Programming (replaces pulp, mip, ortools):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307356418,"data":"  from scipy.optimize import milp, LinearConstraint, Bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307358496,"data":"  import numpy as np\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.30736161,"data":"  res = milp(c=c_vec, constraints=LinearConstraint(A, lb, ub),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307363969,"data":"             integrality=np.ones(n), bounds=Bounds(0, 1))\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307366174,"data":"  # res.success, res.x (solution vector), res.fun (objective value)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307368265,"data":"- Linear Programming: scipy.optimize.linprog(c, A_ub=A, b_ub=b, method=\"highs\")\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307370858,"data":"- Assignment problems: scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment(cost_matrix)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307372982,"data":"- Graph algorithms (matching, shortest path, components): import networkx as nx\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.30737499,"data":"- Constraint satisfaction: encode as ILP via scipy.optimize.milp, or backtracking with pruning\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307376941,"data":"- Number theory: sympy.ntheory or random (Monte Carlo verification)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307378686,"data":"- Geometry: fractions (exact rational) + sympy, avoid floating point\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":454.307380635,"data":"- Game theory/DP: functools.lru_cache for memoized recursion\n"}
